{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1560326-mage-ta-second-edition-or-revised-etc","id":1560326,"title":"Mage: tA: Second Edition or Revised etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-03T15:33:51-07:00","id":1560326,"title":"Mage: tA: Second Edition or Revised etc.","content":"Should I get a hard-copy of the revised or Mage: 2e, book? I already have it, on .PDF; I have M:tA ('92). But, I don't have any hard-copies of the revised WoD-rules (no Vampire, Revised, Mage, Dark Ages (2002), etc. It's like, $60 bucks off of Amazon, and, though, I have more than enough gift cards (like, hundreds I've saved over the years), I'm thinking I should branch out and buy other RPG books (like Dune: 2D20) and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T00:26:26-07:00","id":1560334,"title":"","content":"Why do you want it? There're lots of considerations with getting hard copies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T00:32:14-07:00","id":1560335,"title":"","content":"While they &quot;Why&quot; asked above is most important, some things I can think of that might sway things:<br /> <br /> 1) Revised had a deluxe edition. If you want a physical copy more for display than active use, it's certainly something with some flair over M2e or MRev normal core books.<br /> <br /> 2) If you want something that's just for the experience of reading the physical copy, I'd give an edge to Revised on grounds of layout. M2e has some... iffy decision regarding background elements that can make reading certain pages frustrating (esp. older copies where the text just isn't as crisply printed as it used to be).<br /> <br /> 3) If you plan on using it at the table and want to reference it frequently... which version of the rules you prefer is easily the deciding factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-04T19:42:00-07:00","id":1560359,"title":"","content":"Revised; the latest and greatest White Wolf had before NWoD. And for use at the table; my OG M:tA already disintegrated and I had to replace it. But, I checked out the Revised and, I don't really care for the artwork, though, it's of better quality. <br /> <br /> And why do I want it? I'm hoping it will be a game I will actually play instead of having it sit on my shelf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-05T19:58:58-07:00","id":1560397,"title":"","content":"The more I look into it, the more I am declined; I like some of the Revised books like Dead Magic and Lost Paths; I like the direction they were going; I like the idea of Resonance, but, not even the core-book seems to understand it; I can scratch it in on other-traits for M:tA.<br /> <br /> <br /> And it looks like all Mage the Revised is, is just a change of font. <br /> <br /> And Resonance, but it seems not even M:tA (Revised), understands what that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":2521,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","user":"Iguazu","date":". 06-07-2026, 09:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"